      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sorry about the troll analogy, I guess I was just trying to add a bit of whimsy to the situation. Anyway, let's get down to business.\n\nCalculating the reliability of a flight can be a bit tricky, but there are a few tools you can use to help you out. One option is to check the flight schedules and departure times for both the direct flight and the multi-stop route through Doha or Dubai. You can use flight comparison websites like Skyscanner or Google Flights to compare the two options.\n\nAnother option is to check the airline's website or app for any updates on flight schedules or cancellations. You can also check the airport's website for any information on flight disruptions or delays.\n\nIt's also worth considering the layover times for the multi-stop route. If the layover is too short, it might not be worth it, especially if you're already dealing with a delayed flight. On the other hand, if the layover is long enough, it might be worth it to get to your destination sooner.\n\nFor example, let's say you're looking at a flight from London to Singapore with a layover in Doha. If the layover is only 30 minutes, it might not be worth",
